    "formula_steps": [
      "Use exactly the 120 morning closes at 09:31-11:30 and the 120 afternoon closes at 13:01-15:00; preserve but exclude the standalone 09:30 source row.",
      "Require every used close to be finite and strictly positive. Form 119 adjacent within-morning log returns and 119 adjacent within-afternoon log returns; exclude the 11:30-to-13:01 lunch-break return.",
      "Let RV_am be the sum of squared within-morning log returns and RV_pm be the sum of squared within-afternoon log returns.",
      "Return RV_am/(RV_am+RV_pm) only when total within-half-session realized variance is strictly positive."
    ],
    "formula": "RV_am / (RV_am + RV_pm), where RV_am and RV_pm are sums of squared adjacent log returns within the 120-close morning and afternoon halves",
    "validity": {
      "all_240_required_close_values_finite_and_strictly_positive": true,
      "all_238_within_half_session_log_returns_finite": true,
      "lunch_break_return_excluded": true,
      "total_within_half_session_realized_variance_strictly_positive": true,
      "finite_result_required": true,
      "allowed_closed_interval": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "zero_total_variance_policy": "missing",
      "numerical_endpoint_canonicalization_tolerance": 1e-12,
      "statistical_clipping_imputation_winsorization_or_daily_substitution_allowed": false
    },
    "hypothesis": "A high value means most intraday price uncertainty was expressed in the morning and the afternoon became relatively quiet; earlier price discovery and later stabilization may survive from the next open through the third close.",
    "economic_distinction": "This is a scale-free time-allocation statistic of realized variance. It differs from lower total intraday realized volatility because multiplying both half-session variances by the same positive scale leaves it unchanged, from upside-semivariance share because return signs do not enter, and from terminal location, sign-run order, recovery, VWAP, amount entropy, amount persistence, or amount-weighted efficiency because none of those defines the morning-versus-afternoon variance share.",
    "rejected_before_value_observation": [
      "Lower volatility-resolution share is rejected to avoid a post-result inversion.",
      "Afternoon share, morning-minus-afternoon difference, variance ratio, log ratio, absolute-return ratio, and volatility-level interaction variants are rejected as formula search.",
      "Including the 11:30-to-13:01 lunch return or the ambiguous standalone 09:30 row is rejected.",
      "Opening-only, late-window, unequal-half, rolling, market-relative, industry-relative, amount-weighted, or volume-weighted variants are rejected.",
      "Filling invalid closes, filling zero-total-variance sessions, statistical clipping, winsorization, or daily-price substitution is rejected."
    ]
  },
